<section class="ai-story" id="assistant"><div class="wrap ai-story-grid"><div class="ai-story-copy"><div class="eyebrow">AI that stays with the project</div><h2>Your studio assistant knows what changed and what needs attention.</h2><p>Stonefellow keeps the operational context around the session available across projects, stems, notes, release work and team activity.</p><div class="ai-points"><div class="ai-point"><span class="ai-point-icon">↺</span><div><b>Resume the latest work</b>Return to the current project, version and outstanding tasks instead of starting from scratch.</div></div><div class="ai-point"><span class="ai-point-icon">!</span><div><b>Proactive project intelligence</b>Surface new uploads, missing approvals, overdue follow-ups and release deadlines.</div></div><div class="ai-point"><span class="ai-point-icon">◎</span><div><b>Operational memory</b>Recall prior session notes, mix decisions and project activity when the user asks.</div></div></div></div><div class="assistant-window"><div class="assistant-window-top"><b>Agent Chat · This Is Coming Home</b><span class="assistant-state"><i></i> LISTENING</span></div><div class="assistant-content"><div class="assistant-chat"><div class="assistant-message user">What changed since yesterday?</div><div class="assistant-message agent"><b>Stonefellow</b>Mix v4 was uploaded at 2:14 PM. The bass was lowered 1.5 dB, Taylor approved Vocal v3, and the release checklist is still missing one split-sheet approval.</div><div class="assistant-message user">What should I handle first?</div><div class="assistant-message agent"><b>Stonefellow</b>The split-sheet approval is the most time-sensitive item. Release metadata is due tomorrow, so I would handle those before another mix pass.</div><div class="memory-card"><b>Last session memory</b><div class="memory-line">Drums lowered 1.0 dB</div><div class="memory-line">Vocal v3 approved</div><div class="memory-line">Bridge harmony note saved</div></div></div><aside class="proactive